    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d520">

                <pb facs="0604" n="502" sameAs="frus:frus1933v03/pg502"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">893.50A/42: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in China (Johnson) to the Acting Secretary of
                            State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Peiping</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1933-07-24T10:00:00+08:00">July 24, 1933—10
                        a.m.</date><lb/>[Received July 24—2:25 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>618. Department’s 252, July 21, noon.<anchor n="20" xml:id="d520-f1"/> In this
                    connection please see my 294, March 30, 5 p.m. Rajchman’s connection with League
                    plan will in my opinion doom effort of League to the suspicious attention and
                    opposition of the Japanese.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Johnson</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d520-f1" n="20" xml:id="d520-f1-content">
                <p>Not printed; it reported telegrams No. 138, July 15, 9 p.m., from the Secretary
                    of State, in London, and No. 329, July 18, 5 p.m., from the Ambassador in
                    France.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
